    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d619">

                <pb facs="0636" n="624" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg624"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860P.00/344: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-06-18T14:00:00+03:00">June 18, 1941—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 18—1:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1163. I have received a report that on the night of June 13 the Soviet
                    authorities began mass arrests in Latvia. The arrests appear to be evenly
                    distributed throughout the country. My informant was not in a position to
                    furnish any information concerning the other Baltic States.</p>
                <p>I have also been informed that peasant labor has been requisitioned to speed the
                    completion of a large airport located some 30 miles north of Libau.<anchor
                        n="67" xml:id="d619-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d619-f1" n="67" xml:id="d619-f1-content">
                <p>Liepāja, Libava.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
